Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 09:08:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11244/11362] Decide supervisor exhaustion per level, the axis
 the arms reset on (REQ-ARC-WMTE-7033)

Round three on the earlier agent's exhaustion cell (branch
worktree-agent-a83acaaa5293c1b8f, merged in bd46ce7e65). An adversarial
review found the cell was computed POOLED over the run; confirmed against
source: TrajectorySupervisor.observe clears `_arms_used` on every level-up
("Start the level fresh: arms become available again"), and
`_first_eligible_arm` tests membership in that per-level set. "Every arm
fired" pooled over a run is therefore not "every arm spent on the level
that stagnated". All 5 cells the branch emitted on the live ledger were
false by the axis the code actually uses.

What the branch had right and is kept unchanged: `arms_enabled` on the
receipt with the fired-arm union (REQ-7030), the legacy fallback to the
three default-on arms and the `arms_enabled_source` label, the per-window
state rows and their cap (REQ-7031), the heartbeat fields, the shadow
control pool and `control_matched` (REQ-7032), and the research note.

What changed:

- `_new_arm_cells` now returns (cells, not_decidable). A cell is one
  (receipt, level) where a REQ-7031 window row on that level shows every
  enabled arm already in `arms_used` -- the row's `arms_used` IS the
  per-level set as it stood, so the test is on the reset axis by
  construction. Arms fired elsewhere in the run are never pooled.
- A stagnating receipt with no window rows (every row in the live ledger)
  is listed as not decidable with reason `no_window_rows_recorded`, never
  counted; a receipt whose kept rows are unexhausted but dropped rows past
  the cap is listed with `window_rows_dropped_past_cap`.
- Each cell carries `level`, `arms_fired_on_level`, `exhausted_windows`,
  `windows_on_level`, `first_exhausted_action_index`,
  `level_resolved_by_levelup`, `actions_from_first_exhaustion_to_levelup`,
  and states summarised over that level's rows only. The report prints
  the not-decidable list so zero cells cannot be read as "no level ran dry".
- exp6921's corrected ledger passes the window rows through (it pooled
  redirects too, and its new-arm test needed the rows).
- Spec: REQ-7033 with scenarios A-D; dated CORRECTION notes appended
  under REQ-7030 (retracting SCENARIO-7030-C's first and third bullets)
  and under SCENARIO-6720-6; nothing deleted.

Measured (read-only, results/arc_leaderboard_eval_runs/; 5 applied + 1
shadow receipt with a window, all window 120, seed 20260719): replaying
the supervisor's window arithmetic from the recorded redirect indices and
the level-up frame indices reproduces the recorded redirect boundaries
exactly and the recorded `stagnations_unredirected` on all 6 rows. On that
validated replay: level 0 is exhausted in every applied run (4/4/3/3/4
windows, 18 total), each followed by the level-up at 771-888 that the
shadow run reached with no lever pulled; deeper levels have 0 exhausted
windows (force_exploration_diversity was never spent there; REQ-7040).
The tool, reading receipts alone, emits 0 cells and 5 not-decidable rows
on the live ledger; the ledger has no frame trace and this change does
not ask the tool to re-derive what a receipt did not record.

The input that fires the corrected cell is reachable: SCENARIO-7033-B
drives the real TrajectorySupervisor through the r11l-1408494 timeline
and gets exactly one cell (level 0, 4 windows, resolved 405 actions
later) and none on level 2.

Tests: 120 pass across the seven affected files (was 114). Mutation
proofs follow in the next commit, which records them in the spec.

